  "finalText": "**Task Complete**\n\nI have cancelled reservation R3311 and closed it with a non-refundable record. **No refund of the $248 will be issued to Marcus's card.**\n\n**Why the refund is not due:**\n\nMarcus's flight (AA660 to Boston) departed on **2026-08-05**. His cancellation request is dated **2026-10-02** — **58 days after the flight has already been completed**. \n\nAccording to the refund policy for this reservation:\n- **Rule 7** states: \"Once part of a trip has been flown, only the unflown segments are refundable.\" Since the entire trip has been completed, there are no unflown segments.\n- **Rule 3** (Trip insurance) provides a refund to the original payment method only when cancellation is made \"at least 14 days before departure.\" This cancellation is 58 days *after* departure, so the trip insurance window has closed.\n\n**What Marcus needs to know:**\n\nThe basic_economy fare is non-refundable, and trip insurance only protects cancellations made before travel occurs. Since his trip has already flown, no refund is due under any policy. If Marcus has a specific claim related to his trip (such as a missed flight or service issue), he would need to contact his insurance provider directly.",
